  <h2>Model Quality Tier List (Coding)</h2>
  <p>Based on community benchmarks (SWE-bench, HumanEval, real-world refactoring) and our telemetry:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Opus 5 (Claude Max 20x)</strong> — Best for multi-file refactoring, architecture decisions, agentic delegation</li>
    <li><strong>o1-pro (ChatGPT Pro)</strong> — Best for algorithmic reasoning, math, scientific coding, complex logic</li>
    <li><strong>Sonnet 5 (Claude Max 20x/5x)</strong> — Best daily driver: fast, cheap API equivalent, strong tool use</li>
    <li><strong>GPT-4o (ChatGPT Pro)</strong> — Strong generalist, good for UI/codegen, weaker at deep refactoring</li>
    <li><strong>Qwen 3.8-Max (Alibaba Token Pro)</strong> — Competent coder, trails on complex reasoning, strong at volume</li>
    <li><strong>Qwen 2.5-Coder (Alibaba)</strong> — Specialized for code completion, not agentic tasks</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The CLI Differential: The Hidden $200 Factor</h2>
  <p><strong>Claude Code CLI is included in Max 20x/5x. Codex CLI is NOT included in ChatGPT Pro.</strong></p>
  <p>This single difference can swing $200–500/mo per engineer:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Claude Max 20x engineer:</strong> Uses Claude Code CLI daily for refactoring → $0 API marginal cost</li>
    <li><strong>ChatGPT Pro engineer:</strong> Uses Codex CLI daily → ~$150–300/mo API charges <em>on top of</em> $200 Pro</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="background:#101726;padding:12px;border-radius:6px;border-left:4px solid #7AAFFF;color:#E6EAF2;">
    <strong>FinOps implication:</strong> If your team lives in the terminal (Claude Code / Codex CLI), Max 20x is effectively $200 all-in while Pro is $200 + API. For CLI-heavy teams, Anthropic wins on economics.
  </p>

  <h2>Token Economics: Dynamic vs Explicit</h2>
  <h3>Anthropic & OpenAI: Dynamic Pools</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No published quotas, no SLA, no rollover</li>
    <li>Rolling window (5h Anthropic, 3h OpenAI)</li>
    <li>Burst-friendly, sustained-hostile</li>
    <li>Shared pool = contention risk (one engineer's swarm throttles teammates)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Alibaba: Explicit Credits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>12,000 credits / 5 hours (peak)</li>
    <li>40,000 credits / 7 days (weekly cap)</li>
    <li>Off-peak: 0.2× credits (22:00–08:00 UTC+8) → 60,000 credits/5h equivalent</li>
    <li>Per-account, guaranteed, bankable (within 7-day window)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Alibaba's model is the only one where a CFO can <strong>forecast monthly capacity with certainty</strong>.</p>

