  <h2>Hidden Cost Checklist (All Three)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>☐ <strong>API budget:</strong> Subscriptions ≠ API. Budget 2–3× subscription spend for automation/CI/CD.</li>
    <li>☐ <strong>Reasoning tokens:</strong> o1 reasoning at $60/M output (OpenAI) — monitor per engineer.</li>
    <li>☐ <strong>Prompt caching:</strong> Only API exposes cache discounts (50% o1, 90% Anthropic). Subscriptions opaque.</li>
    <li>☐ <strong>Shared pool contention:</strong> Max 20x and Pro are per-account. Don't concentrate seats on one team/repo.</li>
    <li>☐ <strong>No volume/off-peak (Anthropic/OpenAI):</strong> $200 flat regardless of usage. Alibaba only vendor with time-of-day pricing.</li>
    <li>☐ <strong>Seat = account:</strong> No team pooling in Pro/Max. One subscription per engineer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Migration Path: From Single-Vendor to Mixed</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Audit 30-day actual usage</strong> per engineer: CLI sessions, web sessions, API calls, model mix.</li>
    <li><strong>Classify each engineer</strong> by workload profile (table above).</li>
    <li><strong>Assign primary subscription</strong> per profile. Don't default to one vendor.</li>
    <li><strong>Set up API budget alerts</strong> per engineer (Claude API, OpenAI API, Alibaba API).</li>
    <li><strong>Review monthly:</strong> Utilization %, throttle events, API overflow, productivity signals.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bottom Line for CFOs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No single vendor wins everything.</strong> Best teams mix: Max 20x for refactoring, Pro for reasoning, Token Pro for batch.</li>
    <li><strong>CLI inclusion is the economic swing factor.</strong> Max 20x includes Claude Code; Pro excludes Codex CLI.</li>
    <li><strong>Alibaba Token Pro ($70) is a specialist tool.</strong> 5× value off-peak, explicit credits, but model quality trails.</li>
    <li><strong>API budget > subscription budget.</strong> Plan 2–3× subscription spend for automation/CI/CD.</li>
    <li><strong>Track utilization per seat.</strong> An unused $200 seat is the most expensive idle license in your stack.</li>
  </ul>